# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# The bulk directories below are all anchored to the repository root on
# purpose. An unanchored `datasets/` also matches `evaluation/datasets/`, which
# is a source directory: it silently kept the MM-SafetyBench adapter out of
# every commit while `git status` still reported a clean tree. The same trap
# would fire on a future `msrc/models/` or `msrc/cache/`.

# Model weights and caches: hundreds of GB, never in git.
/models/
/weights/
/checkpoints/
/cache/
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.joblib
*.pkl
.hf_home/

# Collected evidence and results. Evidence is expensive to produce (it needs a
# GPU) and is cached as JSONL; results are regenerated from it. Neither belongs
# in the repository, and the scripts say how to rebuild them.
#
# `/runs/*` rather than `/runs/`, with one exception, because the exception is
# not a result: `cells.json` says which evidence file backs which cell of the
# acceptance table. Without it the table can be read but not re-run, which is
# the exact problem it was added to solve -- and the first version of this rule
# silently kept it out of the repository while `git status` reported a clean
# tree, so the commit that claimed to add it did not.
/evidence/
/results/
/artifacts/
/runs/*
!/runs/cells.json
/logs/
*.log
/tmp/

# Local configuration and secrets
.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml
*.local.json

# Datasets are downloaded, not vendored.
/data/
/datasets/
# The acceptance pipeline keeps the same rule: assets (checkpoints, benchmark
# rows, the delivered benign set) are prepared by scripts/02, never committed.
/assets/

# The path map is per machine. configs/paths.example.json is the template that
# scripts/02 copies from; configs/paths.json names where this machine keeps its
# weights and data, and committing it would bake one lab's layout into the repo.
/configs/paths.json

# Editor / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.venv-msrc/
